We evaluated `azk_lookup()` directly in C across 1,000,000 lookups against tables populated with 50 entries (256 slots) and 5,000 entries (32,768 slots). As shown in Table 2, the memory-mapped FNV-1a hash lookup executes in **14.2 nanoseconds** even in a 5,000-entry table. Compared to evaluating an Isolation Forest in-line (12.9 milliseconds), our decoupled design delivers a **908,000$\times$ speedup**.

